#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179559 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd087cbc-c76f-5900-a1ef-183c383e34ed" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators"}] :question/id #uuid "bcf37a88-0ac3-59ca-8d23-8075f3eab872" :question/math-academy-id "e-9399" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ as $\\dfrac{2}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = \\dfrac{2 - 5}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2 - 5$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2 - 5}{6} = \\dfrac{-3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} =-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ce776ed-33ba-522b-9241-68458339ddc6" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators That Are Not Multiples"}] :question/id #uuid "5b669372-7867-597f-a28f-806aa47fbb2b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9400" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ as $\\dfrac{3}{12}$ and $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ as $\\dfrac{10}{12},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{12} - \\dfrac{10}{12} = \\dfrac{3 - 10}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3 - 10$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f4/f4dc7569aa731c13cf150d867479704cc46cbf7d6502cda4100538b4b2a7e9dc.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 - 10}{12} = \\dfrac{-7}{12} = -\\dfrac{7}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "d8350368-1542-53bc-9275-a1e1ff0a30d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-9401" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - 2\\,\\dfrac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $2 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2 \\,\\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{(2 \\times 3) + 2}{3} = \\dfrac{8}{3}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{8}{3} = \\dfrac{1 - 8}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $1 - 8$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/74/74047d21ae2b703b9962b9655eacbe2eee1a8d94fa4fd36a2924a6b02601d4fa.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1 - 8}{3} = \\dfrac{-7}{3} = -\\dfrac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7}{3} = -2 \\, \\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff50fccc-b442-5847-8029-2ca3be89c018" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "2472cc95-46be-56ac-811c-dd4982bc396f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9403" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12} = \\dfrac{5 - 11}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $5 - 11$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/d9/d9367da101187cf8861458e58f16ea179cff66477d1b9060d3ae199ff8bb3843.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5 - 11}{12} = \\dfrac{-6}{12} = -\\dfrac{6}{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{6}{12} = -\\dfrac{6 \\div 6}{12 \\div 6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff50fccc-b442-5847-8029-2ca3be89c018" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc4f8fd-ffd1-5e06-a562-5ecb24dab1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443733} {:answer/id #uuid "0c063043-348e-5eac-84ed-a7672540af64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443734} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4bc9a3-a0f7-576d-b858-9fdbfa22c852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443739} {:answer/id #uuid "cf2e7900-20db-5d61-9b09-d574171ca258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443802} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8c6b69-277e-56f8-9e05-a7336aec36da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb8c6b69-277e-56f8-9e05-a7336aec36da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443812} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed07ce1b-2e1b-5fc8-98af-e62943422cd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdfbed1a-906b-56f6-99dc-ee6b37df7069" :question/math-academy-id "q-101209" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{7}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{7}{9}=\\frac{2-7}{9}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/bb/bb81cb03e8205a9df3a62ed47ca7b2a4c1a66ad990eaf248f8701480bb2d5bb1.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-7}{9}=\\frac{-5}{9}=-\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd087cbc-c76f-5900-a1ef-183c383e34ed" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e25748-bc23-5fb1-b630-aafea4a149b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443732} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1bfecb-b84d-59ed-91ec-6e4c30f06fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443743} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9f07fa-7338-5059-9ba0-d622dbd68762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443774} {:answer/id #uuid "84e625f5-12e5-520d-b36c-439f88a00f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443777} {:answer/id #uuid "a863f19c-37d5-51d3-bef2-403dae10500a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a863f19c-37d5-51d3-bef2-403dae10500a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443786} :answer-field/id #uuid "4de4f800-0051-5404-8aa0-db9f86428481" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6a01cd3-8e80-578c-a68c-ccfe0c02910d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101213" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\frac{2}{3}$ as $\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{4-5}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-5$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/53/53b1655255807f7007040bb6ba38c2570ec14e0dde04e3d49696953f3750d449.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-5}{6}=\\frac{-1}{6}=-\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd087cbc-c76f-5900-a1ef-183c383e34ed" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59b6dbee-4543-5ac0-bbc5-39ee16ac5735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443761} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb1b3fb-9bee-5812-92ac-c8898be7ff70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443763} {:answer/id #uuid "71439147-1f96-5c48-b484-dc22c9f60c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443770} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ca40b9-8a25-58ad-ac4c-c399c41809a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443785} {:answer/id #uuid "d422ae59-c5ba-5a12-ae7e-8f6ac2487be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6ca40b9-8a25-58ad-ac4c-c399c41809a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443785} :answer-field/id #uuid "c85eb72d-5422-58e8-a29e-633c39efec1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "39ba11e1-e910-5353-9445-994f4bc57a7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-119389" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{7}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\frac{2}{3}$ as $\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{4-7}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/d5/d542609ee447bff7bcb3209bb8ea6eccbd770509d2ae4ad794df9eb6606c2b17.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-7}{6}=\\frac{-3}{6}=-\\frac{3}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{6}=-\\frac{3÷3}{6÷3}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{7}{6}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a275a266-d5d3-5599-9707-0f3c48df54fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177250} {:answer/id #uuid "f8231514-b107-5c9d-bb96-1b41c38a96f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177251} {:answer/id #uuid "254accaa-ba4e-57d5-8013-952e6e54ed0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177253} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8f5c6f-df95-5cfb-9550-a83a1314f99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443746} {:answer/id #uuid "684780d2-2c9c-5628-88dd-65e3f2a4915e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a275a266-d5d3-5599-9707-0f3c48df54fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177250} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c03ac6-fe73-511b-adc0-dfa8540d7eb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "affb9763-c3eb-526b-a6b6-46ddc9c223a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119393" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{5}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+1}{5}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{6}{5}=\\frac{2-6}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/ed/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-6}{5}=\\frac{-4}{5}=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa7dd0d4-32f0-5d93-bd7a-0db7051c395d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177256} {:answer/id #uuid "34b40e63-afd2-58f9-b1cd-05bac05a60a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177257} {:answer/id #uuid "478602a6-4124-5195-96b1-d9ffad534b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443752} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e0f802-017d-573f-8d26-6bcba6dddf07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443796} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e81049-86ab-5d8c-b6c4-344a018e1375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6e81049-86ab-5d8c-b6c4-344a018e1375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443810} :answer-field/id #uuid "998be8cc-960a-5f2e-9c69-31c3ea3d5c9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cafdbddd-e29a-5958-a9cc-7ef04c89f952" :question/math-academy-id "q-119396" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{2}{3}-1\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{5}{6}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{(1\\times 6)+5}{6}=\\frac{11}{6}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{2}{3}$ as $-\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{11}{6}=\\frac{-4-11}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-4-11$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/69/69aec22c2950768abf58a2cae84d3b90a52c79ad44e60d0008605feca272357e.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4-11}{6}=\\frac{-15}{6}=-\\frac{15}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{15}{6}=-\\frac{15÷3}{6÷3}=-\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{5}{2}=-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ce776ed-33ba-522b-9241-68458339ddc6" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators That Are Not Multiples"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68c30aa-09ce-5f14-876c-137da2a53c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177274} {:answer/id #uuid "c525410b-7896-5b81-9798-dd1b48e7605d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177275} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a785dc-9623-5e55-a8eb-536f479e0002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177276} {:answer/id #uuid "3664907b-13e8-5143-8219-e513ad9cadc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177277} {:answer/id #uuid "57a9e501-18d0-5d7b-9eaf-111f7c73d1be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2a785dc-9623-5e55-a8eb-536f479e0002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177276} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e0f5d1-8b02-5903-b123-8eaac410e752" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a153ad0-bfe0-5f41-849a-8736fcf79489" :question/math-academy-id "q-119421" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{3}{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\frac{1}{6}$ as $\\frac{4}{24}$ and $\\frac{3}{8}$ as $\\frac{9}{24},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{24}-\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{4-9}{24}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/3f/3f5b60548cfd0332c74508678de51481f9fa149466c7d7880217b905e4d3891a.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-9}{24}=\\frac{-5}{24}=-\\frac{5}{24}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff50fccc-b442-5847-8029-2ca3be89c018" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bca7a5b-a088-5bcc-802a-8f3860610e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443740} {:answer/id #uuid "2da14132-4d6b-51df-8620-245d7145bdf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443747} {:answer/id #uuid "78d56a67-a62b-5fb2-a31e-0e7c574117ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443772} {:answer/id #uuid "dad1c1cc-d45a-591b-891b-04f549f1712f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443807} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e0dabd-cccc-56f3-88ec-878f11e94828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443815}] :answer-f