n From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators That Are Not Multiples"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8d71d55-26d9-5246-acf4-1fa4aba22737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443787} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ba7c0d-a9b6-5bce-89b2-f81ddd81c18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443791} {:answer/id #uuid "c42d8bbf-060e-5bec-9047-045c39110d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443799} {:answer/id #uuid "d8564b0f-dc6f-53da-bb88-09c871d92f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443806} {:answer/id #uuid "dce90268-d28d-57c3-a229-3c3255e2afbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8564b0f-dc6f-53da-bb88-09c871d92f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443806} :answer-field/id #uuid "89775857-af06-5122-a629-260ef3b33e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b3cacdef-dab0-554e-ba7e-6bcb902467ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-119521" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{9}-\\frac{1}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $-\\frac{1}{9}$ as $-\\frac{2}{18}$ and $\\frac{1}{6}$ as $\\frac{3}{18},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{18}-\\frac{3}{18}=\\frac{-2-3}{18}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-2-3$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f1/f1d24c5635fd9b7523667eb492fe3d88adf1e485b2972e1ba61e3b3d0fb212c5.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2-3}{18}=\\frac{-5}{18}=-\\frac{5}{18}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c778ac-45a7-5054-9e7a-d2aca2969d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443735} {:answer/id #uuid "1132f49f-3789-5224-9661-f88d99141500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443736} {:answer/id #uuid "784d6498-f8d8-591b-8aaf-6809b37ed91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443771} {:answer/id #uuid "cce9891f-2dd1-562f-94b2-7ff3b5e22bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443800} {:answer/id #uuid "ceff5ae7-fcad-552c-a144-b19ffb515812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "784d6498-f8d8-591b-8aaf-6809b37ed91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443771} :answer-field/id #uuid "06b7d979-b715-582b-b778-9506c304818f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1599934d-a927-5358-9a1f-a60248bbf5f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119549" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{3}-1\\,\\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{9}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{(1\\times 9)+1}{9}=\\frac{10}{9}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{1}{3}$ as $-\\frac{3}{9}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{9}-\\frac{10}{9}=\\frac{-3-10}{9}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-3-10$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f2/f27b92c1bbd62f5cba5fc75a4205034a24fb0298e77a662d6c59203dd42a2760.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-3-10}{9}=\\frac{-13}{9}=-\\frac{13}{9}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{13}{9}=-1\\,\\frac{4}{9}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "115b8fee-d484-5ba9-846e-26fb6bd010a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443737} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa215d3-0b57-54ce-a8c7-ad8f3fa77766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443750} {:answer/id #uuid "564f7a03-8298-555e-9435-e9cc345d01e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443759} {:answer/id #uuid "a99e9b36-96e1-51c0-b0ef-9aa47284dd5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443789} {:answer/id #uuid "b05dacd2-7d24-591a-b1c9-f9fd71bb8f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fa215d3-0b57-54ce-a8c7-ad8f3fa77766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443750} :answer-field/id #uuid "49500cf1-dfa6-5c93-8a4f-7807a818ec19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "841f7692-e519-5922-bdbc-38496ec5b53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119552" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{5}-1\\,\\frac{3}{10}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{3}{10}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{(1\\times 10)+3}{10}=\\frac{13}{10}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{1}{5}$ as $-\\frac{2}{10}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{10}-\\frac{13}{10}=\\frac{-2-13}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-2-13$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/65/651e46f49551c462bbf15db5e1fc554aa0ff81d7f81fc64286f15c226be69800.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2-13}{10}=\\frac{-15}{10}=-\\frac{15}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{15}{10}=-\\frac{15÷5}{10÷5}=-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}=-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6f55f6-aa95-5757-97d1-fea7904befd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443755} {:answer/id #uuid "56135516-4bbe-5149-8994-ebb28c6fa458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443758} {:answer/id #uuid "67247274-c78a-5954-a1b1-95cb4632266e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443766} {:answer/id #uuid "83330878-3a8f-572f-8fa3-39627f40a480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443776} {:answer/id #uuid "e97aadf7-8654-534c-ba18-ede197cda907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83330878-3a8f-572f-8fa3-39627f40a480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443776} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f80531f-0b35-5d8e-b16e-de1b40fdee65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38a15d99-3414-508c-84b1-39ed573baedb" :question/math-academy-id "q-119559" :question/problem "Determine the value of $2\\,\\frac{3}{4}-3\\,\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $2\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $3\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(3\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our problem now is to work out the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{13}{4}=\\frac{11-13}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $11-13$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/be/befeb1f1947d5325530ac772fcf1411b04ae74bd78e377dc3eff547461a87627.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{11-13}{4}=\\frac{-2}{4}=-\\frac{2}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{4}=-\\frac{2÷2}{4÷2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd087cbc-c76f-5900-a1ef-183c383e34ed" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "817136bc-e4de-519b-be28-d33e41663843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178673} {:answer/id #uuid "9a03b358-7286-557e-9910-482e4ce46379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178674} {:answer/id #uuid "baa17b0d-816d-5503-a75f-92a2b70b157b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178675} {:answer/id #uuid "1692c879-da3c-5963-b88b-2fd92ba88e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178676} {:answer/id #uuid "458b63ab-0c8c-5ed9-9c1c-b093ad7ae70f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1692c879-da3c-5963-b88b-2fd92ba88e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178676} :answer-field/id #uuid "58c207a8-f286-564f-807f-72d02450ade6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d821b11-e94a-5253-b474-70ced42583fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-42594" :question/problem "$1-\\frac{4}{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We write $1$ as $\\frac{3}{3}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{3-4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3-4$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/42/42e6892273d3fda0560a9b0102077494944812b1e6b66e0bc96af2f0dd2c22c7.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3-4}{3}=\\frac{-1}{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd087cbc-c76f-5900-a1ef-183c383e34ed" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "305de368-fb6e-5bfe-ab1b-de415b87fd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443748} {:answer/id #uuid "50b91276-3486-5538-b2fa-c6c115a6de3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443757} {:answer/id #uuid "61101c93-86b5-562e-8f49-d6ce3915a328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443765} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f07a18-c477-5d57-bb78-0829f09aff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443794} {:answer/id #uuid "cf57b8c3-0bb4-5777-9319-ada83b0f1518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf57b8c3-0bb4-5777-9319-ada83b0f1518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443803} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fba04fc-408e-5dab-9864-4a4edcdd499f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d8f39de-a2f7-5903-8fdc-c4a3db5001e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42713" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\frac{1}{2}$ as $\\frac{2}{4}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}-\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{2-7}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/ee/eea536f581897431a30a8bdadabe7d02fc1f5fc783af2221fda4b2e7f9d6d936.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-7}{4}=\\frac{-5}{4}=-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$"}]}
